        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: спина",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "спина (spiná) — \"the back\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "спина (spiná) — origin disputed. One view takes it from Latin spīna, \"thorn, backbone\", through Old Polish spina, \"backbone\"; Vasmer also allows a native word, a cousin of the Latin one and of Latvian spina, \"a switch\". It is first recorded in the 1600s (Vasmer)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
