          "title": "You'll want to know: язык",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "язык (yazýk) — \"the tongue; a language\". Both meanings, as in English \"tongue\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "язык (yazýk) from Proto-Slavic językŭ, \"tongue\" — inherited, from the old Indo-European word for \"tongue\" that also gave Old Latin dingua, later lingua, and English tongue (Vasmer). The Slavic shape is irregular. \"Language\" grew from the organ, as in English tongue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
