          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кровь (krov) from Proto-Slavic kry, with the stem krŭv- in its other forms — inherited. Vasmer lists Lithuanian kraũjas, \"blood\", Latin cruor, \"gore\", Greek kréas, \"meat\", and Old Norse hrár, \"raw\", so English raw is a cousin, from PIE kréwh₂-, \"raw flesh\"."
            }
